-## Navigation Terms
-
-| Term | Definition |
-| --- | --- |
-| **Observer** | Any bounded actor navigating through projections: a person, a team, an organization, or an AI agent |
-| **Horizon** | Everything the observer can currently see, decide, prove, afford, and govern. Not what is theoretically possible — what is spendable from here. See [Cognitive OS](cognitive-os.md#horizon) |
-| **Affordance** | A path that is visible, reachable, payable, governable, and settleable — all five. Drop one and it is a wish, not an affordance |
-| **Spendable** | Actually actionable from the current position at a payable cost. "Making a problem spendable" means making it clear, evidenced, and bounded enough to act on without pretending |
-| **Capability** | Repeated settlement under variation with reduced orchestration burden. Not explanation, access, imitation, or imagination. One success is evidence; repeated settlement is capability. Its defining signature: **capability frees attention** — the metabolized pathway stops consuming foreground attention, releasing it for better problems (the novice driver attends to the pedals; the expert attends to the road) |
-| **Attention efficiency** | The measured reduction in orchestration load relative to a capability's day-one baseline. The quantitative form of "capability frees attention"; a capability whose attention cost never drops is not promoted. See [math layer](cognitive-os-math-layer.md#capability-promotion) |
-| **Settlement reliability (ρ)** | How trustworthy the feedback from a path is. Unreliable feedback is dampened; capability updates come only from usable or properly dampened settlements. See [math layer](cognitive-os-math-layer.md#settlement-reliability) |
-| **Jump risk** | The priced danger of a large representational leap taken on thin evidence with unreliable feedback |
-| **Twin** | The evolving model of an agent or system, updated after settlement (`TwinUpdated`) |
